    {
      "id": "cymbeline/sceneIV_7.4/p@161468",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "GUIDERIUS.\nThan be so,\nBetter to cease to be. Pray, sir, to th’ army.\nI and my brother are not known; yourself\nSo out of thought, and thereto so o’ergrown,\nCannot be questioned.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIV_7.4/p@161468/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 10,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIV_7.4/p@161468/line-2",
          "start": 11,
          "end": 22,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIV_7.4/p@161468/line-3",
          "start": 23,
          "end": 69,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIV_7.4/p@161468/line-4",
          "start": 70,
          "end": 110,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIV_7.4/p@161468/line-5",
          "start": 111,
          "end": 155,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIV_7.4/p@161468/line-6",
          "start": 156,
          "end": 177,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1210307,
        "end": 1210534,
        "line": 45823,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap07/p@161468",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_7.4"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "GUIDERIUS.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 10
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cymbeline/sceneIV_7.4/p@161699",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "ARVIRAGUS.\nBy this sun that shines,\nI’ll thither. What thing is’t that I never\nDid see man die! scarce ever look’d on blood\nBut that of coward hares, hot goats, and venison!\nNever bestrid a horse, save one that had\nA rider like myself, who ne’er wore rowel\nNor iron on his heel! I am asham’d\nTo look upon the holy sun, to have\nThe benefit of his blest beams, remaining\nSo long a poor unknown.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIV_7.4/p@161699/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 10,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIV_7.4/p@161699/line-2",
          "start": 11,
          "end": 35,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIV_7.4/p@161699/line-3",
          "start": 36,
          "end": 78,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIV_7.4/p@161699/line-4",
          "start": 79,
          "end": 123,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIV_7.4/p@161699/line-5",
          "start": 124,
          "end": 173,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIV_7.4/p@161699/line-6",
          "start": 174,
          "end": 214,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
